IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpfta-types`
IMPORT `cpfta-part3-goods`

-- Tests for Part 3 (ss 13 to 18).  Expectations are read off the text: the contract
-- must be made on or after 1 September 2012 (s 14(1)(c)); the presumption reaches
-- lack of conformity "within the period of 6 months starting after the date" of
-- delivery (s 14(3)); the remedies of ss 15 and 16.

§ `Tests -- Part 3`

-- Non-conforming Goods Facts: kind of contract, deals as consumer (UCTA), transferor claims
-- otherwise, transferor has shown it, contract made on, delivered on, express-term breach,
-- Sale of Goods Act implied-term breach, Supply of Goods Act, Hire-Purchase Act, shown to have
-- existed at delivery, date the lack appeared, established that goods conformed, presumption
-- incompatible with the goods.

GIVEN contract IS A DATE
      delivered IS A DATE
      appeared IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Non-conforming Goods Facts`
`a consumer sale made on` contract `and delivered on` delivered `where the lack of conformity appeared` appeared MEANS
    `Non-conforming Goods Facts` OF `a contract of sale of goods`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, contract, delivered, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, appeared, FALSE, FALSE

§§ `14(1)(c). The contract was made on or after 1 September 2012`

#ASSERT `this Part applies` (`a consumer sale made on` (YMD 2012 9 1) `and delivered on` (YMD 2025 1 10) `where the lack of conformity appeared` (JUST (YMD 2025 2 1)))
#ASSERT NOT `this Part applies` (`a consumer sale made on` (YMD 2012 8 31) `and delivered on` (YMD 2025 1 10) `where the lack of conformity appeared` (JUST (YMD 2025 2 1)))

§§ `14(3). The 6 months starting after delivery`

`the lack of conformity appeared on the day of delivery` MEANS `a consumer sale made on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `and delivered on` (YMD 2025 1 10) `where the lack of conformity appeared` (JUST (YMD 2025 1 10))
`the lack of conformity appeared the day after delivery` MEANS `a consumer sale made on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `and delivered on` (YMD 2025 1 10) `where the lack of conformity appeared` (JUST (YMD 2025 1 11))
`the lack of conformity appeared 6 months after delivery` MEANS `a consumer sale made on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `and delivered on` (YMD 2025 1 10) `where the lack of conformity appeared` (JUST (YMD 2025 7 10))
`the lack of conformity appeared 6 months and a day after delivery` MEANS `a consumer sale made on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `and delivered on` (YMD 2025 1 10) `where the lack of conformity appeared` (JUST (YMD 2025 7 11))
`the lack of conformity appeared, no date known` MEANS `a consumer sale made on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `and delivered on` (YMD 2025 1 10) `where the lack of conformity appeared` NOTHING
`a goods delivered on 31 Aug 2024 and lack appearing on 28 Feb 2025` MEANS `a consumer sale made on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `and delivered on` (YMD 2024 8 31) `where the lack of conformity appeared` (JUST (YMD 2025 2 28))
`a goods delivered on 31 Aug 2024 and lack appearing on 1 Mar 2025` MEANS `a consumer sale made on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `and delivered on` (YMD 2024 8 31) `where the lack of conformity appeared` (JUST (YMD 2025 3 1))

#ASSERT NOT `the lack of conformity appeared within 6 months after delivery` `the lack of conformity appeared on the day of delivery`
#ASSERT `the lack of conformity appeared within 6 months after delivery` `the lack of conformity appeared the day after delivery`
#ASSERT `the lack of conformity appeared within 6 months after delivery` `the lack of conformity appeared 6 months after delivery`
#ASSERT NOT `the lack of conformity appeared within 6 months after delivery` `the lack of conformity appeared 6 months and a day after delivery`
#ASSERT NOT `the lack of conformity appeared within 6 months after delivery` `the lack of conformity appeared, no date known`
#ASSERT `the lack of conformity appeared within 6 months after delivery` `a goods delivered on 31 Aug 2024 and lack appearing on 28 Feb 2025`
#ASSERT NOT `the lack of conformity appeared within 6 months after delivery` `a goods delivered on 31 Aug 2024 and lack appearing on 1 Mar 2025`
#ASSERT `this Part applies` `the lack of conformity appeared the day after delivery`
#ASSERT `this Part applies` `the lack of conformity appeared 6 months after delivery`
#ASSERT NOT `this Part applies` `the lack of conformity appeared 6 months and a day after delivery`

-- 14(4)(a): established that the goods did conform at delivery
#ASSERT NOT `this Part applies` (`Non-conforming Goods Facts` OF `a contract of sale of goods`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, YMD 2020 1 1, YMD 2025 1 10, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, JUST (YMD 2025 3 1), TRUE, FALSE)
-- 14(4)(b): the presumption is incompatible with the nature of the goods or the lack of conformity
#ASSERT NOT `this Part applies` (`Non-conforming Goods Facts` OF `a contract of sale of goods`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, YMD 2020 1 1, YMD 2025 1 10, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, JUST (YMD 2025 3 1), FALSE, TRUE)
-- shown to have existed at delivery: Part applies even after 6 months
#ASSERT `this Part applies` (`Non-conforming Goods Facts` OF `a contract of sale of goods`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, YMD 2020 1 1, YMD 2025 1 10, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, JUST (YMD 2026 1 1), FALSE, FALSE)
-- no breach of any term: the goods conform
#ASSERT NOT `this Part applies` (`Non-conforming Goods Facts` OF `a contract of sale of goods`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, YMD 2020 1 1, YMD 2025 1 10, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, JUST (YMD 2025 2 1), FALSE, FALSE)

§§ `13(3) and 14(1)(a). Dealing as consumer`

-- the transferor claims the transferee does not deal as consumer, and has shown it
#ASSERT NOT `this Part applies` (`Non-conforming Goods Facts` OF `a contract of sale of goods`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2020 1 1, YMD 2025 1 10, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, JUST (YMD 2025 2 1), FALSE, FALSE)
-- the transferor claims it but has not shown it: it is for the transferor to show that
#ASSERT `this Part applies` (`Non-conforming Goods Facts` OF `a contract of sale of goods`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, YMD 2020 1 1, YMD 2025 1 10, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, JUST (YMD 2025 2 1), FALSE, FALSE)
-- no claim, and the Unfair Contract Terms Act answer is that the transferee does not deal as consumer
#ASSERT NOT `this Part applies` (`Non-conforming Goods Facts` OF `a contract of sale of goods`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, YMD 2020 1 1, YMD 2025 1 10, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, JUST (YMD 2025 2 1), FALSE, FALSE)

§§ `13(4). What "does not conform" means, by kind of contract`

--                                                                         kind, UCTA, claims, shown, made, delivered, express, SGA, SoGA, HPA, ...
#ASSERT `the goods do not conform to the applicable contract` (`Non-conforming Goods Facts` OF `a contract of sale of goods`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, YMD 2020 1 1, YMD 2025 1 10, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the goods do not conform to the applicable contract` (`Non-conforming Goods Facts` OF `a contract of sale of goods`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, YMD 2020 1 1, YMD 2025 1 10, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the goods do not conform to the applicable contract` (`Non-conforming Goods Facts` OF `a contract for the transfer of goods`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, YMD 2020 1 1, YMD 2025 1 10, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the goods do not conform to the applicable contract` (`Non-conforming Goods Facts` OF `a contract for the transfer of goods`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, YMD 2020 1 1, YMD 2025 1 10, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the goods do not conform to the applicable contract` (`Non-conforming Goods Facts` OF `a hire-purchase agreement`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, YMD 2020 1 1, YMD 2025 1 10, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the goods do not conform to the applicable contract` (`Non-conforming Goods Facts` OF `a hire-purchase agreement`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, YMD 2020 1 1, YMD 2025 1 10, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE)
-- a breach of an express term counts in each kind of contract
#ASSERT `the goods do not conform to the applicable contract` (`Non-conforming Goods Facts` OF `a hire-purchase agreement`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, YMD 2020 1 1, YMD 2025 1 10, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE)

§§ `13(5). Provisions that do not apply to this Part`

#ASSERT NOT `the provision applies to this Part` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the provision applies to this Part` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the provision applies to this Part` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `the provision applies to this Part` FALSE FALSE FALSE

§§ `15. Repair or replacement of goods`

-- Remedy Facts: impossible, disproportionate to the other remedy, disproportionate to a reduction or rescission.
`a feasible remedy` MEANS `Remedy Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an impossible remedy` MEANS `Remedy Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`a remedy disproportionate to the other remedy` MEANS `Remedy Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`a remedy disproportionate to a reduction or rescission` MEANS `Remedy Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

#ASSERT `the transferee may require the remedy` `a feasible remedy`
#ASSERT NOT `the transferee may require the remedy` `an impossible remedy`
#ASSERT NOT `the transferee may require the remedy` `a remedy disproportionate to the other remedy`
#ASSERT NOT `the transferee may require the remedy` `a remedy disproportionate to a reduction or rescission`

`a Part 3 case` MEANS `a consumer sale made on` (YMD 2020 1 1) `and delivered on` (YMD 2025 1 10) `where the lack of conformity appeared` (JUST (YMD 2025 2 1))
`a case outside Part 3` MEANS `a consumer sale made on` (YMD 2012 8 31) `and delivered on` (YMD 2025 1 10) `where the lack of conformity appeared` (JUST (YMD 2025 2 1))

-- Remedy Claim Facts: transferee requires repair or replacement, which, facts of repair, facts of
-- replacement, transferor did so in a reasonable time without significant inconvenience, transferee
-- rejects and terminates, further requires the other remedy, has given a reasonable time.
`repair required, both remedies feasible, done in time` MEANS `Remedy Claim Facts` OF TRUE, Repair, `a feasible remedy`, `a feasible remedy`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`repair required, both feasible, not done in time` MEANS `Remedy Claim Facts` OF TRUE, Repair, `a feasible remedy`, `a feasible remedy`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`repair impossible, replacement feasible` MEANS `Remedy Claim Facts` OF FALSE, Repair, `an impossible remedy`, `a feasible remedy`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`neither repair nor replacement can be required` MEANS `Remedy Claim Facts` OF FALSE, Repair, `an impossible remedy`, `a remedy disproportionate to a reduction or rescission`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`nothing yet required` MEANS `Remedy Claim Facts` OF FALSE, Repair, `a feasible remedy`, `a feasible remedy`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `the transferee may require the transferor to repair the goods` `a Part 3 case` `repair impossible, replacement feasible`
#ASSERT `the transferee may require the transferor to replace the goods` `a Part 3 case` `repair impossible, replacement feasible`
#ASSERT `the transferee may require the transferor to repair the goods` `a Part 3 case` `nothing yet required`
#ASSERT NOT `the transferee may require the transferor to repair the goods` `a case outside Part 3` `nothing yet required`
#ASSERT NOT `the transferee may require the transferor to replace the goods` `a case outside Part 3` `nothing yet required`

-- 15(2)
#ASSERT `the transferor has met the requirement of section 15(2)(a)` `repair required, both remedies feasible, done in time`
#ASSERT NOT `the transferor has met the requirement of section 15(2)(a)` `repair required, both feasible, not done in time`
#ASSERT `the transferor has met the requirement of section 15(2)(a)` `nothing yet required`
#ASSERT `the transferor must bear the necessary costs of the repair or replacement` `repair required, both remedies feasible, done in time`
#ASSERT NOT `the transferor must bear the necessary costs of the repair or replacement` `nothing yet required`

§§ `16. Reduction in amount to be paid or rescission of contract`

-- 16(2)(a): by virtue of s 15(3) the transferee may require neither
#ASSERT `the transferee may require neither repair nor replacement` `a Part 3 case` `neither repair nor replacement can be required`
#ASSERT NOT `the transferee may require neither repair nor replacement` `a Part 3 case` `repair impossible, replacement feasible`
#ASSERT `the transferee may require a reduction in the amount to be paid or rescind the contract` `a Part 3 case` `neither repair nor replacement can be required`
#ASSERT NOT `the transferee may require a reduction in the amount to be paid or rescind the contract` `a Part 3 case` `repair impossible, replacement feasible`
-- 16(2)(b): the transferee required repair or replacement and the transferor was late or caused inconvenience
#ASSERT `the condition in section 16(2) is satisfied` `a Part 3 case` `repair required, both feasible, not done in time`
#ASSERT NOT `the condition in section 16(2) is satisfied` `a Part 3 case` `repair required, both remedies feasible, done in time`
#ASSERT `the transferee may require a reduction in the amount to be paid or rescind the contract` `a Part 3 case` `repair required, both feasible, not done in time`
-- the transferee cannot use s 16 where this Part does not apply
#ASSERT NOT `the transferee may require a reduction in the amount to be paid or rescind the contract` `a case outside Part 3` `neither repair nor replacement can be required`
-- 16(3): the reimbursement on rescission may be reduced for use
#ASSERT `the reimbursement may be reduced to take account of the use the transferee has had of the goods` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the reimbursement may be reduced to take account of the use the transferee has had of the goods` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the reimbursement may be reduced to take account of the use the transferee has had of the goods` FALSE TRUE

§§ `17. Relation to other remedies, etc.`

`repair required, then goods rejected at once` MEANS `Remedy Claim Facts` OF TRUE, Repair, `a feasible remedy`, `a feasible remedy`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`repair required, then goods rejected after a reasonable time` MEANS `Remedy Claim Facts` OF TRUE, Repair, `a feasible remedy`, `a feasible remedy`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`repair required, then replacement demanded at once` MEANS `Remedy Claim Facts` OF TRUE, Repair, `a feasible remedy`, `a feasible remedy`, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`repair required and the transferee waits` MEANS `Remedy Claim Facts` OF TRUE, Repair, `a feasible remedy`, `a feasible remedy`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `the transferee has acted before giving the transferor a reasonable time` `repair required, then goods rejected at once`
#ASSERT NOT `the transferee has acted before giving the transferor a reasonable time` `repair required, then goods rejected after a reasonable time`
#ASSERT `the transferee has acted before giving the transferor a reasonable time` `repair required, then replacement demanded at once`
#ASSERT NOT `the transferee has acted before giving the transferor a reasonable time` `repair required and the transferee waits`
#ASSERT NOT `the transferee has acted before giving the transferor a reasonable time` `nothing yet required`

§§ `18. Powers of court`

-- Court Power Facts: proceedings seeking a Part 3 remedy, transferee applies for specific performance,
-- transferee requires or claims one remedy, court decides another is appropriate, transferee claimed
-- to rescind, tribunal is a Small Claims Tribunal within its jurisdiction.
#ASSERT `the court may order specific performance of an obligation under section 15` (`Court Power Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the court may order specific performance of an obligation under section 15` (`Court Power Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the court may order specific performance of an obligation under section 15` (`Court Power Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the court may proceed as if the transferee had required the other remedy` (`Court Power Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the court may proceed as if the transferee had required the other remedy` (`Court Power Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the court may proceed as if the transferee had required the other remedy` (`Court Power Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the court may order that the reimbursement be reduced to take account of the use` (`Court Power Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the court may order that the reimbursement be reduced to take account of the use` (`Court Power Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `a Small Claims Tribunal may act under section 18` (`Court Power Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `a Small Claims Tribunal may act under section 18` (`Court Power Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
